'zero behaviour change' claim holds.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["provider_parity.py:585 `parser.add_argument(\"--out\", type=Path, default=None)` — default is already None, not the packaged path","provider_parity.py:630 `if args.out:` gates the only file write; absent `--out`, output goes to stdout (`sys.stdout.write(text)`) and nothing is written","recorded_results_path()/_RESULTS_PATH (:118,:491) is only read by load_recorded_results(), never written by main()","Plan states the story lands with 'zero behaviour change', but resolving a None `--out` to `evals_corpus_root()/provider-parity/provider_parity_results.json` introduces a default on-disk write where none exists today"],"finding":"The plan's provider-parity problem statement — that `--out` defaults to the packaged results file so a client writes into site-packages — contradicts the live code, where `--out` already defaults to None and main() writes only when `--out` is explicitly passed (output is stdout otherwise). The proposed fix would convert today's no-default-write behaviour into a default file write.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff708bc086d8c94bd","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Context: 'provider_parity.py:156 ... --out (:586) defaults to the packaged results file (:118,:491)'; provider_parity.py:585-633","norm_id":"n1bac51d13f08fedb","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A client runs `python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity` with no `--out`: today prints to stdout only; after this change it would create a results file under the corpus root on every run","Operator who relied on stdout-only behaviour now finds unexpected files written"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","c